svg.desc:
Charts for a server-rendered page
Mark links, an open support window and an HTML-friendly shared-domain strip, with their C# source.

1. Give each stacked segment its own destination
   C# source
   Language: csharp
   // Every point owns its ChartMarkOptions.
   var chart =
       ServerRenderedRecipe.LinkedColumns();
   var policy = new VisualSvgOptions("activity")
       .WithFluidWidth()
       .WithFontVariables(
           "--page-font", "--chart-font-size");
   var svg = chart.Prepare(context).ToSvg(policy);
   // Day links stay on this page.
   // Publisher links use NewContext.
   Static chart snapshot:
   Five stacked columns. Updates link to daily summaries; publisher notes open in a new tab.

2. Mark the current row and let open support continue
   C# source
   Language: csharp
   var current = ChartGanttItem.OpenEnded(
       new DateTime(2026, 3, 1));
   series.ReplaceGanttItems(new[] { current });
   series.WithRowOptions(new ChartMarkOptions(
       current: true,
       accessibleLabel: "2026, current"));
   chart.WithGanttOpenEndStyle(
       ChartGanttOpenEndStyle.Fade);
   chart.WithXAxisBounds(
       new DateTime(2026, 1, 1).ToOADate(),
       new DateTime(2027, 1, 1).ToOADate());
   Static chart snapshot:
   Three release rows. The 2026 row is current and its open support bar fades to the right.

3. Keep the label in HTML and share the scale
   C# source
   Language: csharp
   var scale =
       ServerRenderedRecipe.SharedScale();
   // Bounds: 1 Jan 2026 to 1 Jan 2027.
   var row =
       ServerRenderedRecipe.CreateStrip(1);
   var track = row.PrepareStrip(context, scale);
   var axis = scale.PrepareAxis(axisContext);
   var policy = new VisualSvgOptions("release")
       .WithFluidWidth()
       .WithFontVariables(
           "--page-font", "--chart-font-size");
   var svg = track.ToSvg(policy);
   // HTML owns the label. Reuse this scale.
   Static chart snapshot:
   The 2026 release track against the shared January 2026 to January 2027 domain.

Outcomes:
- The chart output and its embedding source are visible
